/T (Identifying entry and exit points: Traders might buy near support levels, anticipating a bounce, and sell near resistance levels, anticipating a pullback. Setting stop-loss orders: To limit potential losses, traders often place stop-loss orders just below support levels \(for long positions\) or just above resistance levels \(for short positions\). Determining trend direction: Observing how the price interacts with support and resistance can help traders understand the prevailing trend.)
/E (Identifying entry and exit points: Traders might buy near support levels, anticipating a bounce, and sell near resistance levels, anticipating a pullback. Setting stop-loss orders: To limit potential losses, traders often place stop-loss orders just below support levels \(for long positions\) or just above resistance levels \(for short positions\). Determining trend direction: Observing how the price interacts with support and resistance can help traders understand the prevailing trend.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
